"Xeno" <XenoTheMorph@gmail.com> wrote:
>I'm trying to add an artifact to my game that gives multiple
>resistances when you are only carying it. I can't seem to add more than
>one, if I try I only get the 'last' one given in artilist.h i.e.
>CARY(AD_FIRE|AD_MAGM) gives Magic res . It seems the code associated
>with them in artifact.c (see below) cannot read both.

I suggest in future that you actually *look* at what a macro does before
modifying what arguments you pass into it... since this would have
revealed immediately that ORing together the AD_foo definitions is
useless.

>What would I have
>to change in the source to allow me to do this? Anyone have any ideas?
>:-)

Yes.  You're going to have to rewrite that code in artifact.c to expect
to read a bit mask from the artifact structure rather than reading a
damage type number, change the artifact structure to make sure the
relevant field is wide enough, create new macros to describe artifact
resistances using a bit mask, and change all the existing entries in
artilist.h to use the bitmask-based method.

I'm a little unclear why you want a multiple-resistances-on-carry artifact,
though, unless you're either refactoring Nethack's resistances model
(which would be a noble goal; a great deal of the tedium in Nethack
can be fairly attributed to the availability of perfect defences and
the concomitant ability to justify "The obscure monster hits with its
incomprehensible attack!  You are instantly slain without regard for
your hit points!" attacks with reference to those perfect defences) or
trying to make (vegetarian) nudists easier to play :-)

I mean, really.  In the late game, an artifact giving multiple
resistances isn't interesting, because you've obtained them from your
diet; in the early game, it's so unlikely to turn up as to be of
no practical relevance in planning overall strategies.
